From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Convert pointer warps to surface-local coordinates

The direct wp_pointer_warp_v1 path passes screen coordinates to
map_point_to_surface(), which only divides by the surface scale. The
window's screen origin must be removed first, as already done for the
locked-pointer position hint and inverted by pointer_handle_motion_internal().

This conversion was lost when pointer warping moved from ClipCursor to
SetCursorPos. For a window with a nonzero origin, a warp is displaced by
that origin or rejected as outside the surface. Repeated cursor recentering
can consequently produce incorrect camera motion.

Subtract the target surface's window origin before scaling. Keep the
absolute pt unchanged for the pending-warp fallback. This does not alter
pointer locking, raw input, resize notifications, or X11.

The original pointer-warp support was implemented by Zakaria Habri.
The subsequent SetCursorPos refactor was by Etaash Mathamsetty; retain both
upstream patches and apply this coordinate correction separately.

Fixes: a10ce92589822114dc8020607926190170f6e8de ("winewayland: Move pointer warp implementation to pSetCursorPos.")
---
diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
@@ -1150,7 +1150,11 @@
             if (data->wayland_surface)
             {
                 wl_surface = data->wayland_surface->wl_surface;
-                surface_pt = map_point_to_surface(data->wayland_surface, pt);
+                /* SetCursorPos uses screen coordinates, but the protocol expects
+                 * surface-local coordinates, just like the locked-pointer hint. */
+                surface_pt.x = pt.x - data->wayland_surface->window.rect.left;
+                surface_pt.y = pt.y - data->wayland_surface->window.rect.top;
+                surface_pt = map_point_to_surface(data->wayland_surface, surface_pt);
             }
 
             wayland_win_data_release(data);
